 ## Overview
-Surf²f is a hybrid neural representation that simultaneously learns an implicit Signed Distance Function (SDF) and an explicit surrogate surface mesh, unified by a shared neural shader for both volume and surface rendering [S1]. It solves the synchronization and efficiency issues inherent in separate implicit and explicit surface representations by maintaining a parallel dual-stream architecture [S1]. Unlike methods that rely solely on SDF volume rendering or static mesh extraction, Surf²f enables real-time interactive rendering of the extracted mesh while leveraging volume rendering for training stability, outperforming NDS, UNISURF, and NeuS in both geometric accuracy and rendering speed [S1].
